DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'MathObjects.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');
TEXT(beginproblem());
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
$prompt = <<'PROMPT_7182_E69F';
<p>7182_e69f</p> <p><strong>Androgen insensitivity syndrome (AIS) </strong> is an X-linked recessive genetic disorder that is caused by a mutation in the AR gene for the human androgen receptor. This results in partial or complete inability of cells to respond to androgens. The disorder affects 1 in 20,000. Individuals affected with AIS have impaired development of male genitals and male secondary sexual characteristics at puberty. The defective gene for AIS is located on the long arm of chromosome X at position 11. </p><p><strong>Achondroplasia </strong> is an autosomal dominant genetic disorder that is caused by a mutation in the FGFR3 gene. This results in a mutated protein that interacts negatively with growth factors leading to complications with bone production. The disorder affects 1 in 27,500 people. Individuals affected with achondroplasia have dwarfism with short arms and legs, an enlarged head, and a prominent forehead. The defective gene for achondroplasia is located on the short arm of chromosome 4 at position 16.3. </p><p>A man (&male;) and a woman (&female;) are planning a family. The man (&male;) has AIS. Genetic testing shows the woman (&female;) is not a carrier for AIS. The man (&male;) has achondroplasia. The mother (&female;) of the man (&male;) does not have achondroplasia. The woman (&female;) has achondroplasia. The father (&male;) of the woman (&female;) does not have achondroplasia.</p><p>Reminder: AIS is X-linked recessive and achondroplasia is autosomal dominant.</p><p>What fraction of their daughters (&female;) will have neither AIS nor achondroplasia?</p>
PROMPT_7182_E69F
loadMacros('parserRadioButtons.pl');
$choice_1 = <<'LITERAL_7182_E69F_CHOICE_1';
None, 0%
LITERAL_7182_E69F_CHOICE_1
$choice_2 = <<'LITERAL_7182_E69F_CHOICE_2';
1/4, 25%
LITERAL_7182_E69F_CHOICE_2
$choice_3 = <<'LITERAL_7182_E69F_CHOICE_3';
1/2, 50%
LITERAL_7182_E69F_CHOICE_3
$choice_4 = <<'LITERAL_7182_E69F_CHOICE_4';
3/4, 75%
LITERAL_7182_E69F_CHOICE_4
$choice_5 = <<'LITERAL_7182_E69F_CHOICE_5';
All, 100%
LITERAL_7182_E69F_CHOICE_5
$correct_1 = <<'LITERAL_7182_E69F_CORRECT_1';
1/4, 25%
LITERAL_7182_E69F_CORRECT_1
@choices = ($choice_1, $choice_2, $choice_3, $choice_4, $choice_5);
$answer = RadioButtons([@choices], $correct_1, labels => 'ABC', displayLabels => 1, randomize => 0, noindex => 1, separator => '<div style="margin-bottom: 0.7em;"></div>');
